WEBVTT

00:11.687 --> 00:14.437
[BORAQCHIN]
The House of Tolui is in ruins.

00:14.527 --> 00:15.647
[♪ drum beats]

00:24.447 --> 00:26.037
[wind blowing]

00:29.827 --> 00:30.867
[BORAQCHIN] Uh?

00:31.537 --> 00:32.827
♪

00:39.667 --> 00:41.387
Oh, it disappeared.

00:42.257 --> 00:43.637
[laughs]

00:43.717 --> 00:46.517
[MÖGE] Boraqchin!
So this is where you are!

00:46.597 --> 00:47.597
[BORAQCHIN] Hmm?

00:47.927 --> 00:50.137
They've got all manner
of gemstones over there.

00:50.227 --> 00:52.597
-Let's go look!
-Gemstones?

00:52.687 --> 00:55.267
Yes! I hear
it's a caravan of traders

00:55.357 --> 00:57.857
that returned from the west.
Come on already!

00:57.937 --> 01:01.237
Wait a moment.
I'm afraid that gemstones

01:01.317 --> 01:03.447
wouldn't look very flattering
on someone like me.

01:03.527 --> 01:04.617
[MÖGE] Mm?

01:06.027 --> 01:07.827
-[MÖGE] So what?
-Uh?

01:07.907 --> 01:10.327
It can be plenty of fun
just to look around.

01:10.407 --> 01:12.367
-[Möge chuckles]
-[BORAQCHIN] Uh...

01:16.707 --> 01:19.877
Hurry up! [chuckles]

01:19.957 --> 01:21.087
♪

01:32.137 --> 01:33.267
[Kirgistani exclaims]

01:35.147 --> 01:36.227
[Boraqchin gasps]

01:37.647 --> 01:38.647
[MÖGE] Look at these.

01:38.727 --> 01:40.027
Don't you think
that we could make

01:40.107 --> 01:41.947
some lovely earrings
out of them?

01:42.607 --> 01:43.947
Yes, they're splendid.

01:44.487 --> 01:46.987
You should try to find something
for yourself, too.

01:47.067 --> 01:49.737
Oh, no, not for me.

01:49.827 --> 01:51.287
[Möge exclaims]

01:58.837 --> 01:59.877
[Boraqchin gasps]

02:01.957 --> 02:04.717
[MAN] I wouldn't bother
with that stone if I were you.

02:05.507 --> 02:06.887
That one somehow
found its way

02:06.967 --> 02:09.757
into the batch of gemstones
we recently procured.

02:09.847 --> 02:11.767
It's honestly a meddlesome stone

02:11.847 --> 02:13.977
that crumbles
whenever it's exposed to light.

02:14.057 --> 02:16.267
Crumbles? In the light?

02:18.147 --> 02:19.567
As if by fate,

02:19.647 --> 02:21.607
I discovered
this shabby-looking rock

02:21.687 --> 02:23.817
amidst the dazzling gemstones,

02:23.897 --> 02:26.947
and found myself
strangely fascinated by it.

02:27.027 --> 02:30.577
A simple stone.
That was how it all began.

02:32.497 --> 02:35.957
[♪ opening theme song playing]

04:14.807 --> 04:16.057
[BORAQCHIN] Uh?

04:16.137 --> 04:18.347
It's coated in a powder.

04:20.847 --> 04:22.057
[sighs]

04:22.937 --> 04:26.397
This hard stone is already
beginning to wear away

04:26.487 --> 04:28.317
in a few days of sunlight.

04:29.357 --> 04:31.067
How curious.

04:32.317 --> 04:33.317
♪

04:34.197 --> 04:35.487
After reading up on it,

04:35.577 --> 04:37.747
I learned this stone
was called sandarac

04:37.827 --> 04:40.997
and was known in the east
for its medicinal properties.

04:41.957 --> 04:43.667
Taken in appropriate doses,

04:43.747 --> 04:46.707
it could heal abscesses
and restore one's vigor.

04:47.127 --> 04:49.757
However, when heated
over a fire,

04:49.837 --> 04:52.757
it turns into a white substance
known as arsenic...

04:54.177 --> 04:56.637
A deadly poison
that dissolves in water

04:56.717 --> 04:59.057
and is devoid of taste or odor.

04:59.677 --> 05:02.767
This brittle rock
unfit to be a gemstone.

05:02.847 --> 05:06.567
It's just...
It's just so fascinating.

05:07.397 --> 05:11.527
In the following year,
Genghis Khan met his demise.

05:12.277 --> 05:13.567
As his consorts,

05:13.657 --> 05:15.737
Möge and I were uncertain
of our fate,

05:15.817 --> 05:19.447
but ended up being taken
as wives by our stepson Ögedei.

05:19.997 --> 05:21.037
And I...

05:21.657 --> 05:25.327
Somehow became
Ögedei's primary empress.

05:26.497 --> 05:29.337
Why did he choose me?

05:29.917 --> 05:33.337
I thought it was simply
because I was the eldest.

05:33.427 --> 05:34.547
But...

05:34.637 --> 05:37.847
Wow! A rock that crumbles
in the light?

05:37.927 --> 05:39.807
[BORAQCHIN]
A trifling hobby of mine.

05:39.887 --> 05:41.687
Please pay it no mind.

05:42.807 --> 05:45.807
Very well. It does seem
beyond my understanding.

05:46.477 --> 05:50.437
That said, I am happy to learn
about something you enjoy.

05:50.527 --> 05:51.737
Please let me know

05:51.817 --> 05:53.607
if there are any other rocks
you would want.

05:53.697 --> 05:55.067
I'll make sure you get them.

05:55.157 --> 05:59.157
Yes. But...
why do so much for me?

06:02.197 --> 06:04.707
[ÖGEDEI] The desire
to obtain something...

06:04.787 --> 06:07.587
That is the urge that sets
the world in motion.

06:07.667 --> 06:08.997
[Boraqchin gasps softly]

06:09.087 --> 06:10.207
♪

06:11.957 --> 06:13.507
I have my own desire.

06:13.587 --> 06:15.927
that this steppe will someday
be a vast market

06:16.007 --> 06:17.637
that connects east and west.

06:18.307 --> 06:19.507
Can you see it?

06:19.597 --> 06:21.597
Eastern and western
cultures alike

06:21.677 --> 06:23.137
passing through to do trade.

06:24.097 --> 06:25.267
In such a world,

06:25.597 --> 06:28.227
we won't need to venture off
to wage war and plunder.

06:28.317 --> 06:30.937
People and goods
will gather here willingly.

06:32.067 --> 06:33.487
[Boraqchin gasps softly]

06:34.487 --> 06:35.777
Thanks for your offer.

06:35.857 --> 06:38.027
I'm really looking
for more books.

06:38.117 --> 06:41.077
I want to learn about the nature
of these stones.

06:41.157 --> 06:42.867
Very well then.

06:43.827 --> 06:46.117
I'm truly glad
you're my empress.

06:46.207 --> 06:47.787
Thank you for accepting.

06:48.877 --> 06:51.377
Tolui and the others
would never understand

06:51.457 --> 06:53.507
what I hope to accomplish.

06:53.587 --> 06:55.507
That's why
I want someone like you

06:55.587 --> 06:58.047
who can truly
appreciate it by my side.

06:58.137 --> 06:59.927
[Boraqchin gasps softly]

07:00.007 --> 07:01.307
♪

07:04.807 --> 07:06.557
[BORAQCHIN]
The House of Tolui's power

07:06.637 --> 07:08.767
will inhibit him
from acting freely.

07:09.557 --> 07:12.147
Can nothing be done about that?

07:12.727 --> 07:14.647
Empress Boraqchin...

07:14.737 --> 07:16.987
Your new physician is here
to see you.

07:17.067 --> 07:18.907
-[Möge chuckles]
-And Lady Möge as well.

07:18.987 --> 07:20.407
Hello!

07:21.197 --> 07:22.987
[PHYSICIAN] Oh, my goodness.

07:23.077 --> 07:24.697
[BORAQCHIN]
I'm quite fond of rocks

07:24.787 --> 07:26.457
that change
appearance and behavior

07:26.537 --> 07:28.167
under heat or light.

07:28.787 --> 07:31.337
Eastern physicians
like yourself are well-versed

07:31.417 --> 07:33.127
in such matters, am I correct?

07:33.207 --> 07:34.877
Indeed.

07:42.177 --> 07:43.257
[Möge breathes softly]

07:43.347 --> 07:45.267
[PHYSICIAN] By any chance,
have you heard

07:45.347 --> 07:47.807
of the Daoist doctrine
known as waidan?

07:47.887 --> 07:49.267
I'm not familiar.

07:49.347 --> 07:52.147
Using fire or water
to refine stones

07:52.227 --> 07:53.477
like these ones,

07:53.567 --> 07:56.237
they tried to concoct elixirs
of immortality.

07:56.737 --> 08:00.777
But inaccurate methods resulted
in a deadly poison instead.

08:01.367 --> 08:02.827
[BORAQCHIN]
It was at this moment

08:02.907 --> 08:05.947
that a plot began
to formulate in my mind.

08:14.297 --> 08:17.297
The physician told me
if I heated this powder,

08:17.377 --> 08:19.467
it would give me arsenic.

08:19.547 --> 08:22.217
Which is lethal in minute doses.

08:23.927 --> 08:25.507
In its sandarac form,

08:25.597 --> 08:27.387
this shouldn't be enough
to kill.

08:28.437 --> 08:30.807
Unlike arsenic,
this doesn't even dissolve

08:30.887 --> 08:32.187
when mixed in water.

08:32.687 --> 08:35.017
Such a truly ungraceful stone.

08:36.147 --> 08:39.357
In that sense, you could say
it is just like me.

08:40.317 --> 08:41.607
♪

08:45.237 --> 08:46.947
[Boraqchin coughing]

08:53.747 --> 08:54.837
I see.

08:54.917 --> 08:57.797
That dose is enough
to cause this?

08:57.877 --> 08:59.797
Now, all that remains...

09:00.417 --> 09:02.547
is to find what cures it.

09:02.637 --> 09:04.717
Sandarac poison leaves the body

09:04.797 --> 09:07.427
after three months
of recuperation.

09:08.137 --> 09:09.807
But was there no faster,

09:09.887 --> 09:12.517
more dramatic remedy
I could use?

09:13.187 --> 09:14.977
One that would seem
like a miracle?

09:16.147 --> 09:20.737
That was my question
when I finally met that girl.

09:21.397 --> 09:22.607
♪

09:32.957 --> 09:34.377
[BORAQCHIN] What do I do?

09:34.747 --> 09:37.087
One false move,
and this plan will put

09:37.167 --> 09:39.507
the Great Kha'an's life
in peril.

09:41.717 --> 09:42.877
[Boraqchin exhales]

09:43.677 --> 09:44.967
[chuckles]

09:45.047 --> 09:48.677
[laughing]

09:50.677 --> 09:53.057
Obviously, I should
entrust all of our fates

09:53.137 --> 09:54.937
into the hands of Tengri,
shouldn't I?

09:58.067 --> 10:01.607
A divination!
We must perform one at once!

10:04.397 --> 10:05.737
[birds chirping]

10:09.447 --> 10:10.407
[SLAVE] Huh?

10:10.907 --> 10:11.957
Here will do.

10:18.957 --> 10:20.547
So is everything prepared?

10:20.627 --> 10:23.717
Oh, well, divinations require
sheep bones,

10:23.797 --> 10:25.047
but we don't have any.

10:25.137 --> 10:27.467
The fire isn't to heat up bones.

10:28.717 --> 10:29.677
[SLAVE] Huh?

10:30.677 --> 10:33.887
Listen well. Cover your nose
and mouth with a cloth.

10:33.977 --> 10:35.637
And don't stand downwind
of the fire.

10:35.727 --> 10:36.647
[SLAVE] Uh?

10:38.767 --> 10:41.647
[BORAQCHIN] Did you not hear me?
Cover yourself at once.

10:41.727 --> 10:42.937
[SLAVE] Oh, right.

10:52.037 --> 10:55.077
[SLAVE] The red powder
is turning white in the fire?

10:55.157 --> 10:56.207
[gasps]

10:57.127 --> 10:58.587
A good omen.

10:59.087 --> 11:00.247
[slave breathes shakily]

11:00.877 --> 11:02.047
[BORAQCHIN] Sure enough.

11:02.337 --> 11:05.467
From there, everything proceeded
exactly as planned.

11:05.547 --> 11:06.967
♪

11:12.757 --> 11:13.807
[inhales]

11:14.347 --> 11:16.977
[Boraqchin exhales]

11:18.187 --> 11:20.607
Yes, all as planned.

11:21.057 --> 11:22.517
-[MÖGE] Boraqchin?
-Uh?

11:23.227 --> 11:25.187
The Great Kha'an is here.

11:27.277 --> 11:29.407
So listen, Boraqchin,

11:29.487 --> 11:31.697
do you remember
what you had said to me?

11:32.447 --> 11:34.537
"To ensure the Mongols
are not divided,

11:35.037 --> 11:37.327
and to ensure
our hearts remain as one."

11:38.077 --> 11:39.917
You said I should take action.

11:41.247 --> 11:44.007
Tell me, have I let you down?

11:46.087 --> 11:49.507
[BORAQCHIN] Möge, you're fine
just the way you are.

11:49.587 --> 11:52.297
As honest and as kind as ever.

11:52.387 --> 11:53.927
But what does that all mean?

11:54.767 --> 11:57.177
Don't you worry about a thing.

11:59.387 --> 12:02.057
If you say so, Boraqchin.

12:05.187 --> 12:06.437
♪

12:06.527 --> 12:07.527
[BORAQCHIN] Möge...

12:08.027 --> 12:09.567
you don't need
to concern yourself

12:09.657 --> 12:11.027
with any of this.

12:11.117 --> 12:14.157
This is a wager
that I've thrown myself into

12:14.237 --> 12:15.787
completely on my own.

12:18.867 --> 12:19.957
[Ögedei chuckles]

12:21.037 --> 12:23.377
[BORAQCHIN] I apologize
for the wait, Great Kha'an.

12:24.037 --> 12:26.047
There's something
you wished to discuss?

12:26.127 --> 12:28.717
Yes, I have a proposal.

12:28.797 --> 12:30.637
It is about that woman.

12:30.717 --> 12:33.427
Tolui's widow,
Sorghaghtani Beki.

12:34.807 --> 12:36.637
-[QADAQ] Get out of here.
-[SITARA] I won't.

12:36.717 --> 12:38.637
Please, leave us!

12:38.727 --> 12:40.557
I won't! I'm sorry!

12:40.637 --> 12:41.517
[Güyük trembling]

12:41.977 --> 12:44.307
I know that you want
to help Lady Töregene.

12:44.397 --> 12:46.107
Today is not the day.

12:46.187 --> 12:47.277
I see.

12:48.437 --> 12:49.487
-[gasps]
-Uh?

12:49.567 --> 12:50.857
[grunts] Wait!

12:51.357 --> 12:54.577
Prince Güyük! Your mother
also means a great deal to me.

12:54.657 --> 12:57.037
Please. If there's
anything you can tell me,

12:57.117 --> 12:58.577
for her sake, you must.

12:58.657 --> 12:59.617
[Güyük trembles]

12:59.707 --> 13:00.997
-[SHIRA] Hey.
-[BOTH] Uh?

13:01.917 --> 13:03.207
So, someone's coming.

13:05.417 --> 13:06.547
Hey!

13:06.627 --> 13:07.667
[Sitara gasps]

13:07.757 --> 13:09.217
I've seen that woman.

13:09.297 --> 13:11.167
She serves under
Empress Boraqchin.

13:11.257 --> 13:12.337
No matter what,

13:12.427 --> 13:14.047
we can't let her find out
we're here.

13:14.137 --> 13:15.257
[SHIRA] What do we do?

13:15.347 --> 13:16.927
[SITARA] Good question.

13:19.017 --> 13:20.977
[ALL] She's here now!
She's here now!

13:21.557 --> 13:22.557
♪

13:24.937 --> 13:26.977
[Güyük groans]

13:27.067 --> 13:28.147
♪

13:38.327 --> 13:39.367
[LADY-IN-WAITING] Hm.

13:40.537 --> 13:43.917
Mm... A good day to you,
Prince Güyük.

13:43.997 --> 13:45.497
And you, Sir Qadaq.

13:45.587 --> 13:48.497
[QADAQ] I trust
Lady Töregene's safe and sound?

13:48.587 --> 13:50.047
[LADY-IN-WAITING] Of course.

13:50.127 --> 13:51.587
In fact, I've come to inform you

13:51.667 --> 13:53.087
that they're all ready
to release her.

13:53.177 --> 13:54.217
[both gasp]

13:54.297 --> 13:55.887
-[LADY-IN-WAITING] Mm?
-[QADAQ] Huh?

13:55.967 --> 13:58.557
[Qadaq groans, sneezes]

13:58.637 --> 14:00.347
Sorry, continue.

14:00.677 --> 14:01.847
Right.

14:01.927 --> 14:04.767
There are a number
of conditions, however.

14:05.147 --> 14:06.307
[SITARA] Conditions?

14:06.397 --> 14:07.557
[LADY-IN-WAITING]
First, Lady Töregene

14:07.647 --> 14:08.977
appears quite weary.

14:09.067 --> 14:10.817
She will spend her time quietly

14:10.897 --> 14:13.197
in Prince Güyük's territory
from now on.

14:13.277 --> 14:14.697
[SITARA]
So they don't want her returning

14:14.777 --> 14:15.737
to the emperor's court?

14:16.367 --> 14:18.077
[LADY-IN-WAITING]
And there's one more thing.

14:18.157 --> 14:21.197
As a final stipulation
of her being released,

14:21.287 --> 14:24.157
the prince must marry
Princess Sorghaghtani.

14:24.247 --> 14:25.457
[gasps]

14:29.747 --> 14:32.047
All right,
we understand your conditions.

14:32.127 --> 14:34.297
But we need to think it over.

14:35.427 --> 14:38.097
Do think carefully
about what's best for her.

14:38.177 --> 14:40.467
And for all of the Mongols
as well.

14:41.137 --> 14:43.057
With that, I must go.

14:45.387 --> 14:47.057
[Güyük trembling]

14:47.147 --> 14:48.307
[sighs]

14:48.397 --> 14:50.187
I'd say you held out quite well.

14:50.267 --> 14:52.027
-Uh...
-[SITARA] Excuse me.

14:52.987 --> 14:54.607
About what she just said...

14:55.567 --> 14:56.737
[Qadaq groans]

14:56.817 --> 14:57.817
[SHIRA] Uh...

14:57.907 --> 14:59.657
[birds squawking]

14:59.737 --> 15:01.157
So, in other words,

15:01.237 --> 15:04.037
all of this is a part
of the Great Khatun's plot.

15:04.117 --> 15:07.077
Her main goal is to weaken
the House of Tolui.

15:07.167 --> 15:10.167
And then vest the Great Kha'an
with more authority.

15:11.167 --> 15:12.547
To accomplish this,

15:12.627 --> 15:15.377
she needed Prince Tolui
to not simply perish,

15:15.467 --> 15:17.507
but to look like
he sacrificed himself

15:17.587 --> 15:18.637
for the Great Kha'an.

15:18.717 --> 15:20.097
[Boraqchin chuckles softly]

15:20.177 --> 15:23.057
That means
the Great Kha'an's ailment was--

15:23.137 --> 15:26.097
Yes. She used Lady Töregene
in her scheme

15:26.177 --> 15:27.267
to give him poison.

15:27.347 --> 15:28.767
One that wouldn't
quite kill him.

15:28.857 --> 15:30.557
[SITARA] Rahj al-gar.

15:30.647 --> 15:32.477
To carry out her plan,

15:32.567 --> 15:34.937
she tested the poison
on herself.

15:35.027 --> 15:36.107
[Ögedei breathes uneasily]

15:36.187 --> 15:38.067
[SITARA]
Using alchemy to orchestrate

15:38.157 --> 15:39.987
people's lives and deaths.

15:40.777 --> 15:42.487
As a witch would.

15:43.997 --> 15:46.907
[QADAQ] And she's even gotten
Prince Güyük involved in this...

15:46.997 --> 15:48.957
making him marry the princess.

15:49.037 --> 15:50.747
[SHIRA]
Nothing to object to, right?

15:50.837 --> 15:53.587
Seems like it's the only way to
bring Lady Töregene back to us.

15:55.047 --> 15:56.547
[Qadaq sighs]

15:56.627 --> 15:59.217
Well, that is true.

16:00.427 --> 16:01.547
Yes, but still...

16:02.097 --> 16:03.347
-[SITARA] Prince Güyük!
-Uh?

16:03.427 --> 16:06.597
Oh, please, please rescue
Lady Töregene.

16:06.677 --> 16:08.017
I beg of you!

16:09.347 --> 16:10.347
[GÜYÜK] Hmm.

16:10.897 --> 16:12.357
[breathes nervously]

16:13.477 --> 16:14.567
[sighs]

16:15.147 --> 16:17.187
-[GÜYÜK] I'll do it.
-[Sitara exclaims]

16:18.647 --> 16:20.157
[bleating]

16:21.067 --> 16:24.527
So long. I should be returning
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

16:24.617 --> 16:25.827
-Hold on.
-Uh?

16:25.907 --> 16:28.657
You cannot tell anyone
what we talked about.

16:29.707 --> 16:31.627
[SHIRA] Understood. [chuckles]

16:31.707 --> 16:33.497
I sure hope so.

16:33.587 --> 16:35.247
You must feel so relieved.

16:35.337 --> 16:36.587
[grunts]

16:36.667 --> 16:38.967
Now you'll be able
to save the one you wanted to.

16:43.047 --> 16:44.797
Thank you, Shira.

16:44.887 --> 16:46.927
It was reassuring
having you here with me.

16:47.557 --> 16:49.597
Um, right, uh, I'm glad.

16:50.187 --> 16:51.307
[chuckles]

16:51.807 --> 16:54.517
Goodbye.
And may Allah preserve you.

16:54.607 --> 16:56.147
Make sure you keep the secret.

16:56.227 --> 16:57.687
Sure, sure.

17:02.697 --> 17:04.157
[HULEGU] What's that?

17:04.237 --> 17:07.237
My mother? Marry Güyük?
Not a chance!

17:07.327 --> 17:08.327
Yes.

17:08.947 --> 17:10.657
That is what the Great Khatun's
messenger was telling me.

17:10.747 --> 17:12.537
It is clear to me
the House of Ögedei

17:12.627 --> 17:14.087
has dropped all pretense.

17:14.167 --> 17:15.627
The lowly son
of the sixth empress

17:15.707 --> 17:17.877
is completely unfit
to marry her.

17:18.167 --> 17:21.547
That may be, but it is what
the Great Khatun wishes.

17:21.627 --> 17:22.797
♪

17:24.257 --> 17:25.387
[SORGHAGHTANI] I see.

17:25.677 --> 17:28.767
[HULEGU] Mother,
you won't accept this, will you?

17:28.847 --> 17:31.937
I refuse to ever call Güyük
my "father."

17:33.807 --> 17:36.647
Mother? Mother? [stutters]

17:36.727 --> 17:37.857
Mother!

17:37.937 --> 17:40.437
[Shira sighs]
She seems pretty spiritless.

17:41.067 --> 17:42.357
Maybe it would've helped

17:42.447 --> 17:44.777
if I mentioned
who killed Prince Tolui, too.

17:46.237 --> 17:48.447
I never thought
Princess Sorghaghtani

17:48.537 --> 17:49.657
would remarry.

17:49.737 --> 17:52.037
Mm. In the near future,

17:52.117 --> 17:54.497
our two houses
will further join hands.

17:55.077 --> 17:56.627
I was about to send a messenger

17:56.707 --> 17:59.127
to go and speak
with the princess.

17:59.837 --> 18:02.757
Well then, in that case,
could you let me have the honor?

18:03.337 --> 18:05.507
-You want to go?
-Yes.

18:06.047 --> 18:08.637
You gave me the book
I've wanted all this time,

18:08.717 --> 18:11.847
which is truly precious
to someone born to scholars.

18:11.927 --> 18:14.557
So, I want to repay
your kindness.

18:14.637 --> 18:15.727
Oh?

18:15.807 --> 18:18.107
I'm well-acquainted
with the princess.

18:18.187 --> 18:21.397
And I feel certain
I can persuade her without fail.

18:21.477 --> 18:23.817
I see. Intriguing.

18:31.117 --> 18:33.657
[SITARA] It's been three years
since last we spoke.

18:33.747 --> 18:37.247
That is the role of someone
who will be empress one day.

18:37.917 --> 18:40.917
[SITARA] Now that the princess
has been reduced to this,

18:41.667 --> 18:44.217
how will she react
when she sees me again?

18:44.547 --> 18:46.007
Will she be angry?

18:46.087 --> 18:47.467
Will she start yelling?

18:48.637 --> 18:50.347
That's fine by me.

18:51.057 --> 18:54.477
The anger I feel towards her
burns far more intensely

18:54.557 --> 18:56.187
than she could imagine.

18:58.057 --> 18:59.107
Pardon me.

19:00.687 --> 19:02.027
[SORGHAGHTANI] Fatima?

19:02.437 --> 19:04.027
It's been so long.

19:04.107 --> 19:07.657
Yes, I've been away
for quite some time now.

19:07.737 --> 19:10.657
Please forgive me.
You see, I... [gasps]

19:12.577 --> 19:13.997
♪

19:15.577 --> 19:19.167
Shira did tell me that
she was terribly despondent.

19:22.047 --> 19:25.007
I am here today as a messenger
for the Great Khatun.

19:26.087 --> 19:28.587
I'm sorry for the loss
of your husband.

19:28.677 --> 19:30.547
I wish there was something
I could have done.

19:30.637 --> 19:31.927
-It's all right.
-Mm?

19:32.387 --> 19:33.717
♪

19:37.267 --> 19:39.107
Please take a look at this.

19:39.647 --> 19:41.937
It's a fine gift
from the Great Khatun.

19:43.187 --> 19:44.107
Also...

19:44.647 --> 19:47.947
I've come to discuss a matter
of great consequence.

19:48.407 --> 19:50.067
One that will affect us all.

19:51.117 --> 19:53.037
Please do not be alarmed.

19:53.487 --> 19:55.327
But I was sent here
because she asks

19:55.407 --> 19:56.697
that you marry Prince Güyük--

19:56.787 --> 19:58.707
-I'll do as she says.
-Uh?

19:59.247 --> 20:00.457
Huh?

20:00.917 --> 20:03.587
[SORGHAGHTANI] If it will serve
the Mongol people in any way,

20:04.167 --> 20:07.087
then do with me as you see fit.

20:08.257 --> 20:10.427
[SITARA] What?
You can't be serious.

20:11.257 --> 20:12.507
[gasps]

20:13.467 --> 20:15.307
Impossible.

20:15.387 --> 20:19.187
You, who robbed me
of everyone I loved...

20:19.267 --> 20:20.437
♪

20:22.437 --> 20:23.727
[indistinct chatter]

20:28.357 --> 20:31.237
You, in all your arrogance...

20:31.317 --> 20:34.827
You gave up hope after losing
someone you cared about?

20:38.157 --> 20:39.407
[Sitara breathes shakily]

20:42.207 --> 20:43.497
What's wrong?

20:44.587 --> 20:45.837
I admire you.

20:46.377 --> 20:48.877
No, I need to look up at her.

20:49.297 --> 20:50.887
I just have to give her a smile,

20:50.967 --> 20:53.097
like I always do.

20:53.677 --> 20:54.847
[breathes shakily]

20:56.517 --> 20:58.517
There is no one left
to protect you.

20:59.517 --> 21:01.937
[panting]

21:04.357 --> 21:06.397
If you want to shut down
and yield to her,

21:06.477 --> 21:07.397
then suit yourself.

21:11.607 --> 21:13.367
But even though
I've lost the ones

21:13.447 --> 21:15.947
who were truly precious to me,

21:16.037 --> 21:17.907
I'll never give up hope.

21:17.987 --> 21:19.657
[Sorghaghtani gasps]

21:20.287 --> 21:21.707
[SITARA] Stop sulking.

21:22.367 --> 21:24.917
I will continue thinking
for myself.

21:25.747 --> 21:26.797
♪

21:33.927 --> 21:37.467
Now then, the matter
at hand is the remarriage

21:37.557 --> 21:39.887
of Princess Sorghaghtani
to Prince Güyük.

21:39.967 --> 21:43.647
Yes, Sorghaghtani Beki
has consented.

21:44.227 --> 21:46.607
Do you have any objections,
Prince Güyük?

21:48.977 --> 21:50.067
[sighs]

21:53.607 --> 21:56.277
I hope this marriage
forges a new bond

21:56.367 --> 21:58.617
between the Houses
of Ögedei and Tolui.

21:59.537 --> 22:00.827
How heartwarming.

22:09.247 --> 22:10.547
[SITARA]
It was unwise for me

22:10.627 --> 22:13.217
to behave as I did with
Princess Sorghaghtani.

22:14.337 --> 22:17.427
Well, I feel certain
we won't ever meet again.

22:17.507 --> 22:18.677
♪

22:21.217 --> 22:22.727
[indistinct chatter]

22:22.807 --> 22:23.767
[SITARA] Mm?

22:24.307 --> 22:25.227
Uh?

22:27.307 --> 22:28.567
[gasps]

22:36.657 --> 22:40.117
Finally, the date of the wedding
ceremony will be set for--

22:40.197 --> 22:41.907
-[SORGHAGHTANI] Wait a moment.
-[BOTH] Uh?

22:41.997 --> 22:43.497
[all exclaim]

22:45.827 --> 22:48.997
I'm afraid
preparations won't be needed.

22:49.087 --> 22:51.047
[MAN 1] Wait.
Princess Sorghaghtani!

22:51.127 --> 22:52.127
[MAN 2] What does that mean?

22:52.457 --> 22:54.087
-[all gasp]
-[MAN] Why won't they be needed?

22:54.167 --> 22:55.547
[gasping]

22:59.257 --> 23:02.597
[SORGHAGHTANI] Sweet Tolui,
I learned what it's like

23:02.677 --> 23:05.727
to lose someone
for the very first time.

23:05.807 --> 23:09.147
[Tolui laughs]

23:09.227 --> 23:11.607
[SORGHAGHTANI]
And to give up all hope.

23:11.687 --> 23:13.897
-[Tolui breathes uneasily]
-[Sorghaghtani cries]

23:15.647 --> 23:17.357
[SORGHAGHTANI] Oh, Tolui.

23:19.277 --> 23:21.947
Do you think
this is how she felt?

23:23.747 --> 23:27.747
I hope you'll forgive me,
Great Kha'an and Great Khatun.

23:28.827 --> 23:30.287
But you see...

23:30.787 --> 23:33.047
I've chosen to decline
this marriage offer.

23:33.127 --> 23:34.167
[Boraqchin grunts]

23:38.677 --> 23:42.637
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next time,
"The Steppe, Ever Unchanging."
